# ---- No server env: this project is client-direct (docs/ADR-0001) ----
#
# There is NO gateway and therefore no server-side environment file. The add-in federates the
# signed-in user's Entra identity to Google (Workforce Identity Federation) in the browser and
# calls Gemini Enterprise directly. No client secret, service-account key, or other credential
# belongs in any env file in this repo.
#
# The add-in's PUBLIC deployment coordinates (project/location/engine, WIF pool/provider, Entra
# tenant/client) live in:
#
#     packages/web-shell/.env.example   ->  copy to packages/web-shell/.env and fill in
#
# Production tenants can also be configured at RUNTIME without rebuilding: host a same-origin
# static /config/<cfg>.json next to the bundle and select it with ?cfg=<name> in the manifest's
# content URL (docs/ADR-0009-tenant-config-bootstrap.md, implemented first slice). Runtime config
# is validated fail-closed and may only override the known public VITE_* keys — never secrets.
